<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>First Contact, 1957</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Ragnar Emsoy&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; October 17th 1957 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Norwegian Coastline, Finnmark area &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; Norway, Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;MTBs are designed for high-speed night-time operations which enables them to get close enough to launch their torpedoes at enemy vessels. With next to no armour, the boats rely upon surprise, speed and maneuverability to avoid being hit by return gunfire.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This fast-paced scenario pits Norwegian MTBs against Soviet MTBs off the rocky Norwegian coastline. The scenario takes place before the advent of anti-ship missiles, and the player has to rely on guns and torpedoes to get the job done. In 1957 the Royal Norwegian Navy still operated a handfull WWII-era destroyers and these are integrated into the Norwegian forces for this encounter.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
